0,Bellari language - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bellari_language,"Bellari (IPA: [beɭːaːri]) was a Dravidian language of India spoken by the Bellara, a Scheduled Caste of Karnataka and Kerala. It is reportedly close to Tulu and Koraga (especially the former), [2] but it is not known if it is a separate language or a dialect of Tulu. [4]",Bellari,Dravidian
1,Bellari language — Grokipedia,https://grokipedia.com/page/bellari_language,"The Bellari language, part of the South-Western Dravidian branch within the broader Dravidian family, exhibits close historical relations to Tulu and Koraga, forming a subgroup often termed Tuluic or encompassing Malekudiya (Kudiya).",Bellari,Dravidian
